@ticketId = 6b053eff649f95570ec0f309
@invalidId = not-a-valid-object-id
@missingId = 674000000000000000000999

### ============================================================================
### 1. CREATE SUPPORT TICKET - POST /api/support/tickets
### ============================================================================

### Create a standard ticket (email_inquiry / callback_request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "email_inquiry",
  "priority": "medium",
  "subject": "Question about ongoing care session schedule",
  "notes": "Could you confirm the timings for next week's scheduled pet care visit?",
  "attachments": []
}

### Create an emergency SOS ticket with optional context references
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "emergency_sos",
  "priority": "critical",
  "subject": "Urgent pet care assistance needed",
  "notes": "Need immediate support regarding an active booking.",
  "booking": "674000000000000000000010",
  "session": "674000000000000000000011",
  "professional": "674000000000000000000012"
}

### Create a wallet / billing or reschedule ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "wallet_billing_inquiry",
  "priority": "low",
  "subject": "Wallet top-up receipt",
  "notes": "Please share an itemized summary for my recent wallet recharge."
}

### Validation check: missing required 'notes' or invalid 'type' enum
# Allowed types: callback_request | email_inquiry | complaint |
#                reschedule_request | wallet_billing_inquiry |
#                concern_report | emergency_sos
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "invalid_type",
  "subject": "Invalid payload test",
  "notes": ""
}

### ============================================================================
### 2. LIST SUPPORT TICKETS - GET /api/support/tickets
### ============================================================================

### List all tickets for the authenticated user
GET {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List tickets filtered by status / type (if supported by your list handler)
GET {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets?status=open&type=email_inquiry
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================================================
### 3. GET SINGLE TICKET THREAD - GET /api/support/tickets/:ticketId
### Marks staff replies as read (updates userLastReadAt) and strips internal notes
### ============================================================================

### Get ticket thread (owner view)
GET {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{ticketId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error 400: Invalid ObjectId format
GET {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{invalidId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Error 404: Non-existent ticket or ticket belonging to another user
GET {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{missingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ============================================================================
### 4. REPLY TO TICKET - POST /api/support/tickets/:ticketId/reply
### Reopens 'resolved' tickets; returns 409 if 'closed' or >= 100 messages
### ============================================================================

### Send a valid reply to an open or resolved ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{ticketId}}/reply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Thanks....... for the update, sharing a quick follow-up detail here."
}

### Error 400: Empty or whitespace-only reply body
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{ticketId}}/reply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "   "
}

### Error 400: Invalid ticketId format on reply
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{invalidId}}/reply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Testing invalid ticket ID"
}

### Error 404: Ticket not found or not owned by current user
POST {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets/{{missingId}}/reply
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Testing missing ticket"
}

### ============================================================================
### 5. AUTHENTICATION GUARD CHECKS (expect 401)
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/support/tickets